=== ★★★★★ THE VALUE LADDER — what this reading MEANS ===
    ★★★★★ bad=0 — REAL COMPUTE AT SCALE. Every one of the N^2 elements matched the
          closed form. ⊘ Note this direction IS a whole-matrix statement: the
          early-exit guard only trips on a MISMATCH, so bad=0 means the verifier
          scanned all N rows. The GR engine ran a full grid and the address plane
          held over every byte of A, B and C.
          maxerr=0 (0 => bit-exact, not merely within tolerance).

